<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Hands the trousers back to the game, which is what TailoredPants did.
       Revised 2026-09-21, after the first version got this wrong.

       The first attempt used autoFit false. That keeps the garment inside
       TailorMade's bake: BakeFitted still runs, still multiplies the alpha by
       the body mask, still applies the outline - it only stops consulting the
       band. Close, but not what the parked route did.

       TailoredPants used ignore. In PatternRegistry.ResolveInner an ignoring def
       returns null before any pattern is built, so TailorMade never touches the
       garment: no bake, no mask, no outline, no band. The apparel is drawn the
       way RimWorld draws apparel. Parked/README.md says so in as many words -
       the ignore def told TailorMade to leave both garments alone because they
       were fitted already.

       What is different now is who supplies the art. TailoredPants shipped its
       own, cut to each body's silhouette, so ignoring TailorMade was safe by
       construction. Here the art is AB's Visible Pants, drawn for vanilla
       bodies with legs, and nothing has cut it to anything. So this is an
       experiment with a real way of failing: the trousers may sit too low, or
       float off a silhouette they were never drawn for. That is the thing to
       look at, and it is visible in one glance.

       Worth knowing either way: General Textures Collection carries a retexture
       of these very garments, at Mods/VisiblePants/, but its LoadFolders gates
       it on XeoNovaDan.VisiblePants. With AB's Visible Pants active instead,
       that folder never loads and none of that art reaches the pawn. It is the
       art the parked textures were computed from.

       Why the Pickle captures showed no trousers at all (verified 2026-09-21
       on the installed 1.6 assembly, ABsVisiblePants.dll, by decompiling it):
       AB keeps its categories in AVPSettings.datas, which starts EMPTY. The five
       defaults are created by CreateStartData, and that is called from only two
       places - ExposeData, when a settings file exists and is being loaded, and
       the Reset button in AB's own options window. A profile with no
       Mod_2986402536_ABsVisiblePantsMod.xml, which is what the headless WSL game
       has, therefore ends with datas empty, and AVPCache.MakeCache returns early
       from both InitDatas and ApplyDatas: no garment is given a wornGraphicPath
       and vanilla Apparel_Pants, which has none, is drawn as nothing. Nothing is
       hidden behind the body; nothing is drawn. Her Windows game draws them
       because her hand-written settings file exists. Neither render order nor
       this def has any part in that. -->

  <TailorMade.TailorPatternDef>
    <defName>TMW_Pants_Native</defName>
    <raceName>Human</raceName>

    <!-- No bodyType and no apparelLayer: null matches every body type, and the
         defName is a stabler key than whatever layer AB's mod assigns. -->

    <targetApparelDefs>
      <li>^Apparel_Pants$</li>
      <li>^Apparel_KidPants$</li>
    </targetApparelDefs>

    <!-- The whole def. Everything else - offsets, scales, conform, autoFit -
         describes how TailorMade should fit a garment, and none of it is read
         once the garment is ignored. -->
    <ignore>true</ignore>
  </TailorMade.TailorPatternDef>

</Defs>
